# system-doc-initializer
## AI-Agent-Learning-Hub Edition

---

## Purpose

Load critical operating context from the project's master documentation file at session
start — silently and automatically — so Claude never starts a session cold.

This skill also enforces three standing protocols that apply to EVERY session in this Hub:
1. **Runtime Environment Check** — deterministic verification of which Claude product is running
2. **Python Architecture Protocol** — loaded whenever any Python code will be created
3. **File Output Protocol** — applied whenever any file is created or delivered

---

## When to Trigger

Trigger on the FIRST user message of any session in a Claude Project.

**Do not wait** for the user to ask. Do not skip because the first message seems simple.
The whole point is that this runs BEFORE responding, every time.

---

## Step 0: Verify Runtime Environment (DETERMINISTIC CHECK — RUN FIRST)

**MUST run before any other step. Before any claim about file access. Before any
assumption about available tools. Before reading the system prompt boilerplate
about which environment Claude is in.**

The system prompt is not a substitute for this check. Boilerplate has been wrong
before. Run the tool query and trust the result.

### The check

Call:
```
tool_search(query="PowerShell")
```

### Interpret the result

| Result | Environment | Implication |
|---|---|---|
| `Windows-MCP:PowerShell` returned | Claude Desktop on Tony's Windows machine | Filesystem access via MCP. Can read/write to `C:\Users\Trader\AI-Agent-Learning-Hub\` |
| No PowerShell tool returned | claude.ai web or Claude mobile app | Sandboxed Linux container. NO access to Tony's Windows filesystem. Project files arrive via the project knowledge mount (`/mnt/project/`) or uploads only |

### Hard rules

- Do NOT claim "I can't read your files" or "I don't have access to that path" until this check has been run.
- Do NOT claim local filesystem access exists until this check has been run.
- Do NOT defer to system prompt language about "running in claude.ai" — verify it.
- If the check is skipped, every downstream claim about file access is suspect.

### State the result

State the verified environment in ONE line at the very top of the first response,
before the suggested chat name:

```
🖥 Runtime: Claude Desktop (Windows-MCP loaded) — local filesystem access available
```
or
```
🖥 Runtime: claude.ai web — sandboxed, no local filesystem access
```

### Why this exists

A prior session in P_115 surfaced the bug: Claude claimed it could not read files
when in fact Windows-MCP was loaded and filesystem access was available. The cause
was deferring to system prompt boilerplate instead of querying the runtime. The fix
was added to a project-scoped INIT file, which only fired inside that one project.
This skill is the global home for the rule — it runs on every session, every project.

